# Game_SortingHat — Team Assignment (ID 7)
# Files: src/coordinator/Game_SortingHat.h, Game_SortingHat.cpp
# HTML: data/game_sorting_setup.html, game_sorting_names.html, game_sorting_run.html

## GAMEPLAY
Harry Potter-style sorting. Press puck → random group assignment.
Pre-filled ticket bag ensures even distribution. 2-8 groups, 2-100 players.

## CONFIG
- numGroups (2-8), targetPlayers (2-100), activePucks (1-3 input pucks)

## STATES
SORT_SETUP → SORT_STARTING (non-blocking 4-beep sequence, ~2.4s) → SORT_RUNNING → SORT_FINISHED

## KEY MECHANICS
- ticketBag: vector of group assignments, drawn randomly
- 1s lockout per puck after each assignment (prevents spam)
- Delayed sound: queued 50ms after light (avoid ESP-NOW packet collision)
- Non-blocking start sequence: 3 short beeps + 1 long, then rainbow
- Last player: puck keeps group color as confirmation
- Bag empty → SORT_FINISHED + fanfare + win effect
- 8 group colors: Red, Blue, Green, Yellow, Magenta, Cyan, Orange, White

## COMMANDS
setup, cfg_groups, cfg_players, cfg_pucks, preview, start, stop, exit

## STATUS JSON
{state, total, done, groups: [count_per_group]}
